PENDING — WORKSHEET RATIFIED (informal/w5-t4-worksheet.md, route (ii): kernel-level cancellation over k, uniform in K/k). Two fears are dead: the Artin-local splitting needs NO henselian machinery (the thickening k[eps]->k is square-zero, so FormallyEtale.comp_bijective does the whole job, and mathlib has no henselian cover-splitting anyway), and the "Hilbert-90 cancellation" dissolves into the already-landed module-level Amitsur exactness (Descent/ModuleDescent.lean:247), because the trunc-exp linearisation happens BEFORE descent, making the descent condition additive. Five bricks T4-a..T4-e; T4-a and T4-c have NO gates and launch immediately.

THE TARGET IS THE SEMILINEAR COMPARISON, NOT A
